## custom_page_document_model_consolidation

### Current Progress

- **Phase 1: Repository and local-tenant truth audit** - ✅ Complete
- **Phase 2: Lightweight production guard and document fixtures** - ⬜ Not started
- **Phase 3: Single backend and frontend document path** - ⬜ Not started
- **Phase 4: Registry and shared-UI simplification** - ⬜ Not started
- **Phase 5: Normalized schema and command retirement** - ⬜ Not started
- **Phase 6: Regression, spec, and lifecycle closure** - ⬜ Not started

### Audit Basis - 2026-08-16

- The normalized feature flags are absent from root and `home` configuration, so
  typed mutations, normalized responses, and normalized reads default off.
- The operator confirmed that none of the backend page-section migration,
  backfill, or cutover commands were run in production; production pages never
  moved away from the legacy `pages.content` document.
- `home` has 7 active JSON-array pages and 23 sections: 20 encoded-string configs,
  3 object configs, 20 numeric IDs, and 3 string IDs.
- Live types include `features` plus `form`, `qa`, `survey`, `poll`, and `vote`.
- The default-off shadow path still accumulated 9 active instances, 4 run rows,
  65 compatibility writes, 4 empty themes, and 1 unresolved quarantine record.
  It has no palette tokens, normalized responses, response migration runs, or
  normalized presets; only 3 active instances belong to matched pages.
- Direct migration/storage/schema/generator/API artifacts total roughly 6,700
  lines, excluding their service, handler, builder, model, spec, and test branches.
- `pages.content` remains the actual browser read/save envelope. Ordinary page
  creates and updates nevertheless call shadow synchronization unconditionally.

### Next Steps

- [ ] Use `.routines/worker` to confirm flags remain off, check only for unexpected
      normalized response rows or palette tokens, and capture the normal backup
      plus a compact content-hash manifest.
- [ ] Add no-loss fixtures for string/object config, numeric/string identity,
      `features`, interactive records, integration sections, and unknown fields.
- [ ] Remove the typed/normalized runtime branches and unconditional shadow writes
      while keeping `PUT /pages/{id}` and locked JSON interactive mutations.
- [ ] Simplify backend/frontend registries and shared UI around the real document
      envelope; retain useful renderer, validation, security, and accessibility work.
- [ ] Remove migration commands, generated contracts, flags, and normalized tables
      only after deployment data proves they are non-authoritative.
- [ ] Run full backend/frontend/migration verification, update specs/routines, and
      retire the superseded typed-page plan pair.

### Safety Gate

- [ ] Do not drop normalized tables in a tenant with an unexpectedly enabled
      normalized flag, normalized-only responses, or nonzero palette tokens.
      Empty shadow and cutover telemetry are disposable implementation residue.

